+# Infrastructure package
+
+`@taxkit/infrastructure` owns TaxKit's Alchemy resource graph and the shared
+contracts used to declare it. The repository-root `alchemy.run.ts` is the thin
+Alchemy host: it supplies Cloudflare providers and state, reads Alchemy's stage
+service, decodes that value, and calls the package's named stack operation.
+
+The package has two public paths:
+
+- `@taxkit/infrastructure/schemas` owns allowed deployment and local stage
+  values and the single stage decoder;
+- `@taxkit/infrastructure/stack` owns the stack and logical resource names,
+  Website Vite policy, resource declaration and safe stack output.
+
+Everything else is private package source. Do not import `src/` paths from
+another workspace.
+
+This is a source-only package because Alchemy and Bun execute the TypeScript
+graph directly. The `source`, `types` and `default` export conditions all point
+to TypeScript source. `build` and `check-types` validate the graph without
+emitting JavaScript or declarations.
+
+Importing the package does not read environment variables, construct a runtime
+or contact Cloudflare. The stack Effect only describes provider work when the
+root Alchemy host runs it under separately authorised provider access.
+
+Run these provider-free focused checks:
+
+```sh
+bun --filter @taxkit/infrastructure check-types
+bun --filter @taxkit/infrastructure test
+```
+
+Passing them proves local package policy and source resolution only. It does
+not prove a plan, deployment, Cloudflare state or public-site behaviour.
